# 基础词 Unit20
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit20核心词汇

{{debate}}{{/dɪˈbeɪt}}{{n./v. 辩论；讨论}}{{The students held a debate on climate change.}}
{{decade}}{{/ˈdekeɪd}}{{n. 十年}}{{The city has changed dramatically over the past decade.}}
{{decline}}{{/dɪˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 下降；拒绝}}{{The company's profits have declined significantly.}}
{{dedicate}}{{/ˈdedɪkeɪt}}{{v. 奉献；致力于}}{{She dedicated her life to helping the poor.}}
{{deficit}}{{/ˈdefɪsɪt}}{{n. 赤字；不足；亏损}}{{The government is trying to reduce the budget deficit.}}
{{define}}{{/dɪˈfaɪn}}{{v. 定义；限定}}{{How do you define success?}}
{{deliberate}}{{/dɪˈlɪbərət}}{{adj./v. 故意的；深思熟虑的}}{{It was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.}}
{{delicate}}{{/ˈdelɪkət}}{{adj. 精致的；脆弱的；微妙的}}{{The vase is very delicate, so handle it with care.}}
{{demonstrate}}{{/ˈdemənstreɪt}}{{v. 展示；证明；示威}}{{The experiment demonstrates the effect of gravity.}}
{{deny}}{{/dɪˈnaɪ}}{{v. 否认；拒绝}}{{He denied any involvement in the scandal.}}
{{depict}}{{/dɪˈpɪkt}}{{v. 描绘；描述}}{{The painting depicts a beautiful landscape.}}
{{derive}}{{/dɪˈraɪv}}{{v. 源于；获得}}{{The word is derived from Latin.}}
{{design}}{{/dɪˈzaɪn}}{{n./v. 设计；计划}}{{The architect presented the design for the new building.}}
{{desire}}{{/dɪˈzaɪər}}{{n./v. 渴望；欲望}}{{He has a strong desire to succeed in life.}}
{{desperate}}{{/ˈdespərət}}{{adj. 绝望的；不顾一切的}}{{The refugees were in desperate need of food and water.}}
{{despite}}{{/dɪˈspaɪt}}{{prep. 尽管；不管}}{{Despite the rain, the event was a great success.}}
{{detect}}{{/dɪˈtekt}}{{v. 发现；探测}}{{The sensor can detect changes in temperature.}}
{{determine}}{{/dɪˈtɜːmɪn}}{{v. 决定；确定}}{{Your attitude determines your altitude in life.}}
{{devote}}{{/dɪˈvəʊt}}{{v. 献身于；致力于}}{{She devoted her life to helping the poor.}}
{{dimension}}{{/daɪˈmenʃn}}{{n. 维度；尺寸；方面}}{{The problem has several dimensions that need to be considered.}}
{{diminish}}{{/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ}}{{v. 减少；缩小}}{{His influence has diminished over the years.}}
{{discipline}}{{/ˈdɪsəplɪn}}{{n./v. 纪律；学科；训练}}{{Self-discipline is the key to success.}}
{{disclose}}{{/dɪsˈkləʊz}}{{v. 揭露；透露}}{{The company refused to disclose its financial information.}}
{{discrimination}}{{/dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃn}}{{n. 歧视；辨别}}{{Racial discrimination is illegal in many countries.}}
{{dismiss}}{{/dɪsˈmɪs}}{{v. 解雇；驳回；不理会}}{{The court dismissed the case due to lack of evidence.}}
{{disorder}}{{/dɪsˈɔːdər}}{{n. 混乱；疾病}}{{The patient was diagnosed with a sleep disorder.}}
{{display}}{{/dɪˈspleɪ}}{{v./n. 展示；显示}}{{The museum displays artifacts from ancient civilizations.}}
{{dispose}}{{/dɪsˈpəʊz}}{{v. 处理；布置；使倾向于}}{{Please dispose of the waste properly.}}
{{dispute}}{{/dɪˈspjuːt}}{{n./v. 争论；纠纷}}{{The dispute between the two companies was settled in court.}}
{{dissolve}}{{/dɪˈzɒlv}}{{v. 溶解；解散}}{{Sugar dissolves quickly in hot water.}}
{{distinguish}}{{/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ}}{{v. 区分；辨别}}{{It is hard to distinguish the twins from each other.}}
{{distribute}}{{/dɪˈstrɪbjuːt}}{{v. 分配；分发}}{{The volunteers distributed food to the homeless.}}
{{diverse}}{{/daɪˈvɜːs}}{{adj. 多样的；不同的}}{{The university has a diverse student body.}}
{{domestic}}{{/dəˈmestɪk}}{{adj. 国内的；家庭的}}{{Domestic flights are cheaper than international ones.}}
{{dominant}}{{/ˈdɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 占主导地位的；显著的}}{{English is the dominant language in international business.}}
{{draft}}{{/drɑːft}}{{n./v. 草稿；起草}}{{She submitted the first draft of her thesis.}}
{{dramatic}}{{/drəˈmætɪk}}{{adj. 戏剧性的；巨大的}}{{There has been a dramatic change in the weather.}}
{{durable}}{{/ˈdjʊərəbl}}{{adj. 耐用的；持久的}}{{This material is very durable and can last for years.}}
{{dynamic}}{{/daɪˈnæmɪk}}{{adj. 动态的；有活力的}}{{The city has a dynamic and vibrant culture.}}
{{elaborate}}{{/ɪˈlæbərət}}{{adj./v. 精心制作的；详细阐述}}{{Could you elaborate on your proposal?}}
{{eliminate}}{{/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt}}{{v. 消除；淘汰}}{{We must eliminate all errors before publication.}}
{{embrace}}{{/ɪmˈbreɪs}}{{v./n. 拥抱；接受}}{{The company embraced new technology to improve productivity.}}
{{emerge}}{{/ɪˈmɜːdʒ}}{{v. 出现；浮现}}{{New evidence emerged during the investigation.}}
{{emit}}{{/ɪˈmɪt}}{{v. 发出；排放}}{{The factory emits large amounts of carbon dioxide.}}
{{emphasis}}{{/ˈemfəsɪs}}{{n. 强调；重点}}{{The teacher placed emphasis on critical thinking.}}
{{enable}}{{/ɪˈneɪbl}}{{v. 使能够；使可能}}{{Technology enables us to communicate across the globe.}}
{{encounter}}{{/ɪnˈkaʊntər}}{{v./n. 遇到；遭遇}}{{We encountered many difficulties during the trip.}}
{{endure}}{{/ɪnˈdjʊər}}{{v. 忍受；持续}}{{She endured years of hardship before achieving success.}}
{{enforce}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 执行；强制}}{{The police enforce the law to maintain order.}}
{{engage}}{{/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ}}{{v. 从事；吸引；订婚}}{{She is engaged in scientific research.}}
{{enhance}}{{/ɪnˈhɑːns}}{{v. 提高；增强}}{{Exercise enhances both physical and mental health.}}
{{enormous}}{{/ɪˈnɔːməs}}{{adj. 巨大的；庞大的}}{{The project requires an enormous amount of investment.}}
{{ensure}}{{/ɪnˈʃʊər}}{{v. 确保；保证}}{{Please ensure that all doors are locked before leaving.}}
{{enterprise}}{{/ˈentəpraɪz}}{{n. 企业；事业}}{{The enterprise has grown into a multinational corporation.}}
{{enthusiasm}}{{/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm}}{{n. 热情；热心}}{{He showed great enthusiasm for the project.}}
{{entire}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪər}}{{adj. 整个的；全部的}}{{The entire family gathered for the holiday celebration.}}
{{entitle}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪtl}}{{v. 给予权利；给…命名}}{{This ticket entitles you to a free meal.}}
{{environment}}{{/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt}}{{n. 环境；自然环境}}{{Protecting the environment is everyone's responsibility.}}
{{equivalent}}{{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt}}{{adj./n. 等同的；等价物}}{{One mile is equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}
{{establish}}{{/ɪˈstæblɪʃ}}{{v. 建立；确立}}{{The university was established in 1905.}}
{{estimate}}{{/ˈestɪmeɪt}}{{v./n. 估计；评价}}{{The cost is estimated at two million dollars.}}
{{evaluate}}{{/ɪˈvæljueɪt}}{{v. 评估；评价}}{{The committee will evaluate all the applications.}}
{{evidence}}{{/ˈevɪdəns}}{{n. 证据；迹象}}{{There is strong evidence to support the theory.}}
{{evolve}}{{/ɪˈvɒlv}}{{v. 进化；发展}}{{Languages evolve over time.}}
{{exaggerate}}{{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt}}{{v. 夸张；夸大}}{{He tends to exaggerate his achievements.}}
{{exceed}}{{/ɪkˈsiːd}}{{v. 超过；超越}}{{Sales exceeded expectations this quarter.}}
{{exclude}}{{/ɪkˈskluːd}}{{v. 排除；排斥}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}
{{execute}}{{/ˈeksɪkjuːt}}{{v. 执行；处决}}{{The plan was executed perfectly.}}
{{exhaust}}{{/ɪɡˈzɔːst}}{{v./n. 使筋疲力尽；废气}}{{The long hike exhausted everyone.}}
{{exhibit}}{{/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt}}{{v./n. 展示；展览品}}{{The museum exhibits rare paintings from the 18th century.}}
{{expand}}{{/ɪkˈspænd}}{{v. 扩大；膨胀}}{{The company plans to expand into Asian markets.}}
{{explicit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 明确的；清楚的}}{{The instructions must be explicit and easy to follow.}}
{{exploit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt}}{{v./n. 开发；利用；功绩}}{{We should exploit renewable energy resources.}}
{{explore}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔːr}}{{v. 探索；考察}}{{They explored the ancient ruins in the jungle.}}
{{expose}}{{/ɪkˈspəʊz}}{{v. 暴露；揭露}}{{The report exposed corruption in the government.}}
{{extend}}{{/ɪkˈstend}}{{v. 延伸；扩展；给予}}{{The deadline has been extended by one week.}}
{{extent}}{{/ɪkˈstent}}{{n. 程度；范围}}{{To what extent do you agree with this statement?}}
{{external}}{{/ɪkˈstɜːnl}}{{adj. 外部的；外面的}}{{The external walls of the building need repainting.}}
{{extraordinary}}{{/ɪkˈstrɔːdnri}}{{adj. 非凡的；特别的}}{{She has extraordinary talent in music.}}
{{extreme}}{{/ɪkˈstriːm}}{{adj./n. 极端的；极度}}{{Extreme weather events are becoming more frequent.}}
{{facilitate}}{{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt}}{{v. 促进；使便利}}{{Technology facilitates communication between people.}}
{{factor}}{{/ˈfæktər}}{{n. 因素；因子}}{{Several factors contributed to the success of the project.}}
{{feature}}{{/ˈfiːtʃər}}{{n./v. 特征；以…为特色}}{{The phone has many new features.}}
{{federal}}{{/ˈfedərəl}}{{adj. 联邦的}}{{The federal government passed a new tax law.}}
{{feedback}}{{/ˈfiːdbæk}}{{n. 反馈；回馈}}{{We welcome feedback from our customers.}}
{{figure}}{{/ˈfɪɡər}}{{n./v. 数字；人物；计算；认为}}{{The figure shows a steady increase in population.}}
{{finance}}{{/ˈfaɪnæns}}{{n./v. 财政；资助}}{{The government needs to improve its finance management.}}
{{flexible}}{{/ˈfleksəbl}}{{adj. 灵活的；可变通的}}{{The company offers flexible working hours.}}
{{flourish}}{{/ˈflʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 繁荣；茂盛}}{{The business has flourished under new management.}}
{{focus}}{{/ˈfəʊkəs}}{{v./n. 集中；焦点}}{{Please focus on the main points of the lecture.}}
{{forecast}}{{/ˈfɔːkɑːst}}{{v./n. 预测；预报}}{{The weather forecast predicts rain tomorrow.}}
{{formal}}{{/ˈfɔːml}}{{adj. 正式的；正规的}}{{The invitation requires formal attire.}}
{{foundation}}{{/faʊnˈdeɪʃn}}{{n. 基础；基金会}}{{Education is the foundation of a successful career.}}
{{framework}}{{/ˈfreɪmwɜːk}}{{n. 框架；结构}}{{The government established a new legal framework.}}
{{fraud}}{{/frɔːd}}{{n. 欺诈；骗子}}{{He was convicted of financial fraud.}}
{{frustrate}}{{/frʌˈstreɪt}}{{v. 使沮丧；挫败}}{{The lack of progress frustrated the team.}}
{{fulfil/fulfill}}{{/fʊlˈfɪl}}{{v. 履行；实现；满足}}{{She fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.}}
{{function}}{{/ˈfʌŋkʃn}}{{n./v. 功能；运转}}{{The main function of the heart is to pump blood.}}
{{fund}}{{/fʌnd}}{{n./v. 基金；资助}}{{The university received a large fund for research.}}
{{fundamental}}{{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl}}{{adj. 基本的；根本的}}{{Freedom of speech is a fundamental human right.}}
